.TH YHTPS 1 "2026" "YhHTTPServer 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yhtps \- YhHTTPServer, a zero\-config static and framework HTTP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yhtps
.B s
.I PATH
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B yhtps
.B sf
.I PATH
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yhtps
serves static files and built framework output (Vite, Next.js export,
SvelteKit, Astro, plain HTML) straight from the filesystem. It is a single
native binary with no runtime dependencies and runs on Linux, macOS, Windows
and Android/Termux.
.PP
It covers the same ground as the npm packages
.B http-server
and
.BR serve .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B s
Serve a file or a directory. The path is auto\-detected: a directory is served
with index\-file lookup and (by default) directory listings; a file is served
at
.BR / .
.TP
.B sf
Serve a framework build folder. Adds client\-side routing (SPA fallback) and
clean URLs: unknown paths return the fallback file, and
.B /about
is served from
.B about.html
when it exists.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Port to listen on. Default: 5050.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-address " " \fIADDRESS\fR
Address to bind. Default: 0.0.0.0 (all interfaces).
.TP
.B \-\-clean
Disable request logging.
.TP
.B \-\-silent
Suppress all output, banner included.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cache " " \fISECONDS\fR
Cache\-Control max\-age. \-1 disables caching. Default: 3600.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-gzip
Enable gzip compression.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-brotli
Enable brotli compression. Preferred over gzip when the client allows both.
.TP
.B \-\-compress\-threshold \fIBYTES\fR
Minimum size worth compressing. Default: 1024.
.TP
.B \-\-cors
Send permissive CORS headers.
.TP
.B \-\-cors\-origin \fIORIGIN\fR
Custom Access\-Control\-Allow\-Origin value. Implies \-\-cors.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-open
Open the served URL in the default browser.
.TP
.B \-\-spa
Force SPA fallback: unknown paths serve the fallback file.
.TP
.B \-\-fallback \fIFILE\fR
SPA fallback file. Default: index.html.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-listing
Disable directory listings.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-index " " \fIFILE,...\fR
Index file names to try in a directory. Default: index.html,index.htm.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-extensions " " \fIEXT,...\fR
Extra extensions to try for extension\-less requests, e.g.
.B \-e html
serves
.B /about
from
.BR about.html .
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-proxy " " \fIURL\fR
Proxy requests to this origin. Without \-\-proxy\-prefix it acts as a fallback:
anything that is not a file on disk is forwarded upstream.
.TP
.B \-\-proxy\-prefix \fIPATH\fR
Only proxy paths starting with
.IR PATH ,
e.g.
.BR "\-\-proxy\-prefix /api" .
Everything else is served locally, so SPA routing keeps working.
.TP
.B \-\-username \fIUSER\fR
HTTP Basic auth user name.
.TP
.B \-\-password \fIPASS\fR
HTTP Basic auth password.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-ssl
Serve over HTTPS. A self\-signed certificate is generated when none is given.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-cert " " \fIFILE\fR
TLS certificate chain, PEM.
.TP
.BR \-K ", " \-\-key " " \fIFILE\fR
TLS private key, PEM.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-range
Disable byte\-range requests.
.TP
.B \-\-timeout \fISECONDS\fR
Connection header read timeout.
.TP
.B \-\-header "\fIName: Value\fR"
Extra response header. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-format \fIFORMAT\fR
One of
.BR pretty " (default), " short ", " combined ", " json .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable coloured output. Also honoured via the NO_COLOR environment variable.
.TP
.B \-\-trust\-proxy
Trust X\-Forwarded\-For / X\-Real\-IP when determining the client IP.
.SH EXAMPLES
Serve a single static page:
.PP
.RS 4
yhtps s /var/www/html/index.html
.RE
.PP
Serve a Vite build on port 8080 and open a browser:
.PP
.RS 4
yhtps sf /var/www/html/blog/dist/ \-p 8080 \-o
.RE
.PP
Serve quietly, with compression and CORS:
.PP
.RS 4
yhtps s ./public \-\-clean \-\-gzip \-\-brotli \-\-cors
.RE
.PP
Serve an SPA and proxy its API:
.PP
.RS 4
yhtps sf ./dist \-P http://127.0.0.1:3000 \-\-proxy\-prefix /api
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown.
.TP
.B 1
Startup failure: bad path, port already in use, invalid certificate, and so on.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README and BUILDING.md for cross\-compilation recipes.
